@startuml

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
}

actor "Admin" as User
participant "AdminPage" as UI
participant "AccountController" as Controller
participant "AccountService" as Service
participant "AppUserRepository" as Repo
participant "BookingRepository" as BookingRepo
database "Database" as DB

== UC-07: View customer accounts ==

User -> UI : 1. Open People & access
activate User
activate UI

UI -> Controller : 2. GET /api/account/users?role=Customer
activate Controller

Controller -> Service : 3. users("Customer")
activate Service

Service -> Service : 4. requireAdmin()
activate Service
deactivate Service

alt Admin is authorized
  Service -> Repo : 5. findAll()
  activate Repo

  Repo -> DB : 6. SELECT Customer accounts
  activate DB
  DB --> Repo : 7. Customer accounts
  deactivate DB

  Repo --> Service : 8. Repository result
  deactivate Repo
else Authorization fails
  note over Service,Controller
    Non-admin -> 403
    The service propagates ApiException to ApiExceptionHandler.
  end note
end

Service --> Controller : 9. Customer directory or propagated error
deactivate Service

Controller --> UI : 10. HTTP 200 or mapped 4xx
deactivate Controller

User -> UI : 11. Choose View for a Customer
UI -> Controller : 12. GET /api/account/users/{id}/activity
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : 13. activity(userId)
activate Service
Service -> BookingRepo : 14. Load recent bookings
activate BookingRepo
BookingRepo -> DB : 15. SELECT booking and issue history
activate DB
DB --> BookingRepo : 16. Activity rows
deactivate DB
BookingRepo --> Service : 17. Recent activity
deactivate BookingRepo
Service --> Controller : 18. Read-only Customer details
deactivate Service
Controller --> UI : 19. Activity response
deactivate Controller

UI -> UI : 20. Open read-only View modal

UI --> User : 21. Show profile, bookings, and issues

deactivate UI
deactivate User

@enduml
